---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="lx-page-head">
    <p class="lx-kicker">Resume</p>
    <h1 class="lx-title-lg">Profile</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 lx-prose-quiet">
    Harvard student studying Pure Mathematics and Computer Science with interests in Applied AI, Software Engineering,
    and Research. Currently conducting research on LLM interpretability and steering vectors at Harvard's Cognitive, Cognition,
    and Development Lab under Post Doc Peng and Professor Ullman. Experienced entrepreneur and engineer with proven track
    record of building impactful products and organizations. Co-founded multiple ventures including Libertas Debate Academy
    (6-figure revenue) and IvyLine (500 users in 5 days). Passionate about using technology to democratize access to
    education and opportunities.
  </div>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Education</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="A.B., Pure Mathematics and Computer Science"
      subtitle="2024 to March 2028 at Harvard University, Cambridge, MA"
    >
      Relevant coursework: Introduction to Statistics (110), Proof-based Linear Algebra (22a), Data Structures and Algorithms (120), Reinforcement Learning and Optimal Control (158)
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Boston Latin School"
      subtitle="Graduated 2024, Boston, MA"
    >
      Six years on Speech & Debate. NSDA National Student Leadership Council member, representing 50,000+ student members. 3x DECA International Career Development Conference qualifier — a school record.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Experience</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Undergraduate Researcher at Harvard Ullman Lab"
      subtitle="September 2025 to Present at Harvard University, Cambridge, MA"
    >
      Working with Post Doc Peng on Steering Vectors for LLM safety and interpretability. Using text of the law versus spirit of the law experiments to test LLMs. Use FARSC and SLURM to run evals for frontier models.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Campus Lead at Cursor"
      subtitle="September 2025 to Present at Cursor, Cambridge, MA"
    >
      Selected as one of 40 campus leads across U.S. colleges. Hosted HackMIT x Cursor and Harvard x Cursor events, expanding campus engagement and developer adoption.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Co-Founder at Libertas Debate Academy"
      subtitle="September 2023 to Present, Remote"
    >
      Achieved six-figure revenue in first year of operation. Managed team of 16 USA National Champions; led curriculum for 40 students and summer camp for 25. Led National Coaching, Debate Camps, and Online Classes; students earned Gold TOC bids and won NCFL Nationals. Oversaw SEO optimization, marketing at national debate tournaments, client and coach calls, hiring, and operations.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Founder & Engineer at IvyLine"
      subtitle="June 2024 to Present, Remote"
    >
      Built IvyLine Search, a full-stack web app democratizing college advice; scaled to 500 users in 5 days with 100K LinkedIn impressions. Reduced callback authentication speed by 180%; deployed over 20,000 lines of production code. Developed semantic search for 200+ opportunities using Grok 3, Xenova embeddings, and Vercel; achieved 5-figure revenue (Sept. 2024 – May 2025).
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Senior Software Engineer at Harvard Tech for Social Good"
      subtitle="February 2024 to Present at Harvard University, Cambridge, MA"
    >
      2024: Built a full-stack RAG app for the CDC NIOSH team to analyze thousands of pages on mining safety. 2025: Co-leading project with Wikimedia (294B yearly views) improving accessibility via JAWS assistive tech.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Co-Founder & Board Member at Outreach Debate"
      subtitle="August 2022 to Present, Remote"
    >
      Founded international 501(c)(3) nonprofit — the world's largest student-run debate organization — growing from 6 to 300+ members across 20+ countries and 50 states. Organized camps serving 1,500+ debaters, saving over $1.5M collectively; raised $4,000+ for initiatives. Partnered with the Coolidge Foundation to host the Coolidge Qualifier, a national tournament awarding a bid to the Coolidge Cup; received publicity from the National Speech and Debate Association.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Massachusetts Lead at Encode Justice"
      subtitle="March 2022 to September 2024, Remote"
    >
      Mobilized state-level AI safety advocacy with ACLU MA and local legislators. Authored policy memo for Senator Warren's team and contributed to memo sent to Senator Schumer.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Awards</h2>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>Elks Most Valuable Student (Top 2.7%)</li>
    <li>Coolidge Scholarship Finalist (Top 0.03%)</li>
    <li>NHS Scholarship Recipient (Top 3.5%)</li>
    <li>Vanderbilt Chancellor's Scholarship Recipient</li>
    <li>Top 6 Public Forum Debater in USA; 9x National Qualifier (2x Gold TOC, 4x NSDA Nationals, 3x NCFL Grand Nationals); 7 career TOC bids</li>
    <li>Elimination rounds at national championships in four formats: Public Forum, Congress, World Schools, and Policy</li>
    <li>Top Speaker, Milo Cup; 2nd Speaker, Sunvitational; 5th Speaker, Harvard Round Robin</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Writing & Press</h2>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>Contributing writer, International Policy Digest</li>
    <li>Bylines in Dig Boston and the L.A. Times High School Insider</li>
    <li>Profiled in The Argo: "Spotlight on Sam Chen"</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Activities</h2>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>Harvard Intellectual Vitality Student Advisory Board</li>
    <li>Asian American Dance Troupe</li>
    <li>Harvard Undergraduate Foreign Policy</li>
    <li>Asian American Christian Fellowship</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="lx-section-head">
    <h2 class="lx-title-lg">Skills</h2>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>Python</li>
    <li>JavaScript</li>
    <li>TypeScript</li>
    <li>Rust</li>
    <li>React</li>
    <li>Next.js</li>
    <li>Node.js</li>
    <li>TensorFlow</li>
    <li>PyTorch</li>
    <li>Machine Learning</li>
    <li>LLM Research</li>
    <li>NLP</li>
    <li>Full-Stack Development</li>
    <li>Vercel</li>
    <li>Git</li>
    <li>SLURM</li>
    <li>Data Structures</li>
    <li>Algorithms</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
